{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>המנדים</b> — He mentioned המתאוים (those who reject). It would be הוי המתאוים, because among them were people for whom the thing the prophet prophesied was in doubt — perhaps he will not fulfill his word. And some of them say: he prophesied rarely, and this is המנדים, those who push far away, and 'you bring near the seat of violence,' for שבת, like מושב זקנים יושבי שער. And since you are מנדים, pushing far away in your hearts the day of calamity, saying: the time has not yet arrived and the time is not near, you do not fear to sin, and you bring near the seat of violence at the gate to judge violence — pushing far away the evil day and bringing near a seat of violence."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The comment opens by glossing המנדים with המתאוים (those who reject/despise), then shifts to reading it as 'those who push far away' (מרחיקים). The syntax of the final clause is compressed and the argument elliptical; rendered hyper-literally to preserve Ibn Ezra's terseness. The word שבת is read as 'seat' in the sense of מושב."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:20.389575952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}